{
  "slug": "university-admissions-checklist",
  "title": "University Admissions Checklist",
  "subtitle": "Your Step-by-Step Guide to Winning Admits at Top Global Universities",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Why an Admissions Checklist Matters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Applying to top universities is overwhelming: multiple deadlines, essays, test scores, and recommendation letters all competing for your attention. Without structure, it’s easy to miss opportunities."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "An admissions checklist is your **blueprint**—it ensures you don’t just apply, but apply with strategy and excellence. Every top admit—Harvard, Oxford, INSEAD, ISB—requires clarity, storytelling, and discipline."
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Reflection",
          "text": "Write why you want to pursue higher education—career pivot, leadership growth, or global exposure.",
          "lines": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Define Your Target Programs & Career Goals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Before you chase rankings, get clear on goals."
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Do you want consulting post-MBA? Target INSEAD, Kellogg, LBS.",
            "Do you want finance? Look at Wharton, Columbia, ISB.",
            "Do you want tech/product? Consider Stanford, Berkeley Haas."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write your short-term (post-program job) and long-term (10-year career vision) goals.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "",
              "My goal"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Short term (first job after the programme)",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Long term (10-year vision)",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Shortlisting Universities – Dream, Target, Safety",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Use the **DTS Framework**:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "**Dream Schools:** Aspirational (Harvard, Oxford, INSEAD).",
            "**Target Schools:** Competitive but realistic.",
            "**Safety Schools:** Solid chances of admission."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "List 2–3 universities under each bucket.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "Dream",
              "Target",
              "Safety"
            ],
            "rows": 3
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 2"
    },
    {
      "title": "Understanding Admission Requirements",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Each university evaluates 4 dimensions:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "**Academics:** GPA, transcripts.",
            "**Test Scores:** GMAT, GRE, IELTS/TOEFL.",
            "**Professional Experience:** Impact, leadership.",
            "**Application Materials:** Resume, essays, recommendations."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Pick 1 target school and list its admission requirements.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "Requirement",
              "What the school asks for",
              "My status"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Academics",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Test scores",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Experience",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Resume, essays, recommendations",
                "",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 3"
    },
    {
      "title": "Building a Strong Resume for Admissions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Admissions resumes differ from job resumes. They must highlight:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Leadership & initiative.",
            "Impact with quantified metrics.",
            "Academic and extracurricular achievements."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "example",
          "items": [
            "Instead of “Worked on audit projects” → “Led 3-member team on Fortune 500 audit, improving reporting accuracy by 15%.”"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Rewrite one of your resume bullets for admissions.",
          "lines": 4
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 4"
    },
    {
      "title": "Crafting Your Personal Statement/Essays",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Essays = storytelling. They answer:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Why this program?",
            "Why now?",
            "Why you?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Framework: Past → Present → Future.",
            "Example: Past = finance background, Present = interest in ESG, Future = global ESG leader."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 3 sentences connecting your past, present, and future into a story.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "",
              "My story"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Past",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Present",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "Future",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 5"
    },
    {
      "title": "Letters of Recommendation – Strategy & Guidance",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Recommendations should validate your story."
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Pick recommenders who **know you**, not just senior titles.",
            "Provide them a draft with examples of your leadership.",
            "Ensure consistency with your essays."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "List 2 people who can write authentic recommendations for you.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "Recommender",
              "How they know me"
            ],
            "rows": 2
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 6"
    },
    {
      "title": "Preparing for Standardized Tests",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "**GMAT/GRE:** Practise quant and verbal daily. Aim at or above the median in each school’s latest class profile.",
            "**IELTS/TOEFL:** Focus on fluency + writing clarity.",
            "Start prep at least 6–9 months before deadlines."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write your target GMAT/GRE score and exam date.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "Test",
              "Target score",
              "Exam date"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "GMAT / GRE",
                "",
                ""
              ],
              [
                "IELTS / TOEFL (if needed)",
                "",
                ""
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 7"
    },
    {
      "title": "Application Timelines & Deadlines",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Typical timelines:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Round 1: September–October.",
            "Round 2: January–February.",
            "Round 3: around April."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Worksheet",
          "text": "Create a 12-month calendar marking test dates, essay deadlines, and application submissions.",
          "lines": 4,
          "table": {
            "columns": [
              "Month",
              "Tests",
              "Essays",
              "Submissions"
            ],
            "rows": 12,
            "widths": [
              16,
              28,
              28,
              28
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 8"
    },
    {
      "title": "Preparing for Admissions Interviews",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Universities test: communication, clarity, fit.",
            "Common questions:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "Why MBA/Masters now?",
            "Why this school?",
            "Tell me about a leadership experience."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Record yourself answering 1 question. Time yourself—stay under 2 minutes.",
          "lines": 4
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 9"
    },
    {
      "title": "Financing Your Education",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Options:"
        },
        {
          "t": "ul",
          "items": [
            "**Scholarships:** Merit, need-based.",
            "**Loans:** Prodigy Finance, MPower, local banks.",
            "**Grants:** Some universities provide research or assistantship roles."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "exercise",
          "label": "Exercise",
          "text": "Write 2 scholarship/loan options you’d explore.",
          "lines": 4,
          "numbered": 2
        }
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Step 10"
    },
    {
      "title": "Worked examples",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "lines",
          "items": [
            "**An Indian business school admit:** Riya, a chartered accountant from a Big Four firm, refined her essays around her leadership impact. She won an admit with a scholarship.",
            "**A UK MBA admit:** Arjun, a former strategy consulting analyst, reframed his resume and essays around his social impact goals, and prepared hard for the interview."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "callout",
          "label": "Lesson",
          "text": "Clarity + Storytelling + Proof of Impact wins."
        }
      ],
      "example": true
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes and Your 90-Day Plan",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "avoid",
          "items": [
            "Copy-pasting essays across schools.",
            "Overemphasizing GPA while ignoring leadership.",
            "Missing deadlines by poor planning."
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "plan",
          "rows": [
            [
              "Days 1–30",
              "Shortlist + Resume."
            ],
            [
              "Days 31–60",
              "Essays + Recommendations."
            ],
            [
              "Days 61–90",
              "Interview prep + submissions."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
